 "response": "Volidrox's budget is now **$1,626K**.\n\n**How the withdrawals were resolved**\n\nMany withdrawals form chains, where a later withdrawal cancels an earlier one. I worked each chain back from the latest withdrawal. The withdrawal at the end of a chain stays in force, and each step back alternates between in force and cancelled. For example:\n- **#0003 (\u2212$196K) counts.** #0146 withdraws #0026, which brings back #0015. #0015 withdraws #0004, so #0003 is no longer withdrawn.\n- **#0023 (+$352K) does not count.** #0842 withdraws #0136, which brings back #0030, and #0030 withdraws #0023.\n- **#0313 (+$32K) does not count.** The chain #1583 \u2192 #1280 \u2192 #0919 \u2192 #0489 \u2192 #0335 ends with #0335 in force, and #0335 withdraws #0313.\n- **#0056 (\u2212$549K) counts.** The six-step chain from #0910 down to #0069 ends with #0069 cancelled, so #0056 stands.\n\n**Calculation**\n\n1. The starting budget is $2,760K (#0001).\n2. Updates that end up withdrawn are left out. Among them are #0002, #0047, #0102, #0152, #0215, #0360, #0949, #1330 and #1420, along with roughly 110 others.\n3. All remaining increases and decreases are applied in record order.\n4. The running total ends at $1,626K after the last budget update, #1597 (\u2212$140K).\n\nThe total depends on many hand-traced steps, so a slip in one chain or addition would change it.\n\nANSWER: $1626K",
